ht bg, illustration (178×260) prominent, headline \"Pay / Manage / Grow…\" one word per line (so \"Pay\\nManage\\nGrow…\"), subcopy \"An easy app to manage all your payment and finance-related needs\", primary button \"Get Started\" (links to 02), secondary \"Sign in\", \"Already have an account?\" text before Sign in. Status bar + home indicator.\n\nLayout: \n- Status bar (47h)\n- Illustration centered\n- Headline big\n- Subcopy\n- Spacer\n- Get Started button (full width)\n- \"Already have an account? Sign in\" row\n- Home indicator\n\n2. **02_Phone_Number** — sheet over 01_Onboarding. So the frame contains: dimmed 01_Onboarding behind + bottom sheet with header \"Get Started\", sub \"Please enter the mobile phone number\", actions Cancel / Get Started, phone field with +91 prefix, focused state, placeholder 9812345678, numeric keypad open at bottom.\n\nFor the sheet-over presentation: I need 01_Onboarding content dimmed behind. I can build frame 02 as: a copy of onboarding screen (simplified or actual instance) + dark overlay + white sheet + keypad.\n\nSince I need to prototype: 02 Get Started → 03_Home; Cancel → 01_Onboarding.\n\nI'll construct 02 by creating a frame that contains an instance of a reusable \"Onboarding screen content\" or just recreate the background content. Simpler: create a component \"Screen/Onboarding Content\"? That may complicate. Alternative: in frame 02, add a copy (detached) of the onboarding layout as background, dim it with a black overlay at 40%, then the sheet.\n\nTo reuse, I can make frame 01_Onboarding, then for 02 create a new frame and place a *copy* of 01's children. Using the Plugin API I can clone nodes. But cloning from another page frame into 02... frames must be top-level on the page. I can clone 01_Onboarding as a regular frame nested inside 02? A clone of a top-level frame becomes a frame that I can append into 02 frame. That works: clone, remove prototype stuff, resize/reposition, set as background.\n\nActually simpler