tiles, actions, banner, transaction rows, scan button, side menu, button/text-field states as reusable components. To satisfy \"Component reuse\" evaluation without excessive complexity, I'll create components in the workspace for: \n- Btn/Primary (Get Started), Btn/Secondary (Sign in), Btn/Ghost? \n- Field/Phone (focused)\n- Home/Header\n- Home/BalanceCard\n- Home/AccountTile (component, 4 instances)\n- Home/ActionButton (Send/Receive variants — could be one component with variants; simpler: one component, instances with overrides)\n- Home/OfferBanner\n- Home/TransactionRow (3 instances)\n- Menu/Row (5 instances)\n- Menu/SideMenu\n\nCreating components then instantiating them in frames is more work but scores points. Given tool-call budget concerns (rate limit hit a couple times but seems intermittent), I'll be pragmatic: create key reusable components (AccountTile, TransactionRow, MenuRow, ActionButton, Button variants) and build the rest directly. Actually let me create a decent set since \"Component reuse\" is a graded criterion.\n\nLet me think about the rate limit: I hit \"tool call limit\" errors intermittently on the Enterprise plan but retries succeeded. I should minimize calls and batch big operations per use_figma call. Each use_figma call can run a big script (up to 50k chars). I'll aim for ~6-8 use_figma calls + screenshots.\n\nLet me define the design system concretely:\n\nColors:\n- brand/primary: #1E32FA\n- brand/dark: #1423B8 (pressed)\n- brand/tint: #EEF1FF (light tint backgrounds)\n- ink/900: #0E1330 (headings)? Keep simpler: text/primary #121417? Let me pick:\n  - text/primary: #101828\n  - text/secondary: #667085\n  - text/tertiary: #98A2B3\n  - bg/app: #F6F7FB\n  - surface: #FFFFFF\n  - border: #E4E7EC\n  - success: #12B76A\n  - error/negative: #F04438\n  - dark card (balance): deep navy gradient? Balance card: brand gradient #1E32FA → #4452FF? Gradients allowed. I'll do a rich brand card with subtle gradient and white text.\n- scrim: #0B0F19 at 48%\n\nType scale (Inter):\n- Display: 34/Bold (onboarding headline)\n- H2: 22/Semi Bold\n- Title: 17/Semi Bold\n- Body: 15/Regular (line 22)\n- Body strong: 15/Semi Bold\n- Caption: 13/Regular, 13/Medium\n- Micro/label: 11/Medium, letter-spacing 0.06em uppercase for section labels\n- Balance: 34/Bold ₹85,625\n\nRadii: 12 cards, 16 sheet top, 999 pills, buttons 14.\nElevation: card shadow 0 1 2 rgba(16,24,40,0.06); sheet 0 -8 24 rgba(16,24,40,0.16).\n\nSpacing: 4pt grid, page padding 20.\n\nNow detailed layouts.\n\n### 01_Onboarding (390×844), bg #FFFFFF? Let's use white with brand tint circle behind illustration? Keep clean: white bg.\n\n- Status bar instance at top (0,0, 390×47). On white bg, default dark glyphs — given component likely dark glyphs; fine.\n- Illustration: instance of 4:5 (178×260), maybe scale up ~1.3 → 232×338. Place centered at y≈110. Maybe add soft brand-tint circle behind (decorative).\n- Headline \"Pay\\nManage\\nGrow…\" — Display 34 Bold, at y≈470, left-aligned x=24? Or centered. The brief: copy \"Pay / Manage / Grow…\" one word per line. Centered or left — designer's choice. I'll center everything: illustration center, headline center, subcopy center.\n- Subcopy: \"An easy app to manage all your payment and finance-related needs\" 15/Regular secondary, centered, width ~320.\n- Bottom: Get Started button (instance of given Button 1:23, resized to 350×52, label \"Get Started\"), y≈660.\n- Row: \"Already have an account?\" + \"Sign in\" link text. Brief lists actions \"Get Started\" · \"Sign in\" and copy \"Already have an account?\". I'll render as a single centered row: gray \"Already have an account?\" + brand \"Sign in\". y≈732.\n- Home indicator at bottom (y=844-34=810).\n\nCheck the given Button component default label — need to inspect. It's a symbol 358×52. I'll check its text via get_design_context? I don't have that tool — only metadata, screenshot, use_figma. use_figma can inspect properties programmatically. I'll inspect inside the build script and adapt: find text node in instance and set characters.\n\nSame for Text Field component (358×77, includes label \"Phone Number\"? probably label + field). I'll inspect and adapt: set label \"Phone Number\", placeholder \"9812345678\", add +91 prefix. The given text field may not have a prefix slot. Since \"focused\" state with country code is required and the given is default-only, I'll build my own Field/Phone component (that's expected: states are mine to design). But \"Reuse the components in 02 · Components\" — I should use the Text Field at least as base. Hmm, the focused phone field with +91 prefix — I'll construct a custom field component (Field/Phone) that visually matches the default Text Field style (I'll inspect its colors/radius) and set state focused with brand border + cursor.\n\nPlan: In script, inspect Button and Text Field structure (names, fills, text), then decide. To save calls, I'll inspect in the same call that builds 01, reading properties and applying overrides generically: find first TEXT in instance → set \"Get Started\"; set instance size via resize (instances support resize if component has constraints... may distort. Component is 358×52; I need 350×52 — close; I can resize instance; if constraints are fixed, text stays centered hopefully).\n\nRisk: overriding text in component instance requires fonts loaded. Fine.\n\nFor Sign in: text link, no button component needed.\n\n### 02_Phone_Number (390×844)\n- Clone of 01_Onboarding contents as background (the whole frame, scaled 1:1), then scrim rgba(11,15,25,0.48) full-frame.\n- Sheet: white, top radius 24? (16-24), from y≈300 down to above keypad? Layout: sheet contains:\n  - grabber? optional small\n  - Header row: \"Get Started\" 22 SemiBold + Cancel text button right? Actions: \"Cancel\" · \"Get Started\". Typical: title left, Cancel right (text button). Sub \"Please enter the mobile phone number\".\n  - Phone field: label \"Phone Number\", field box with \"+91\" prefix (with divider), placeholder \"9812345678\" gray, focused border brand 2px, cursor after prefix? Field empty & focused → caret visible before placeholder? Placeholder shows since empty. Caret typically hidden when empty in static mockups; I'll add a small caret bar before placeholder? If field is empty with placeholder, no caret. But \"focused\" state: brand border + maybe subtle ring. Good enough.\n  - Button \"Get Started\" primary full width.\n  - Numeric keypad instance (390×226) at bottom — sheet includes keypad? Keypad is system UI 390 wide, 226 tall, positioned at y=844-226-home indicator? Given keypad 226 tall. Home indicator overlays or sits below keypad. Typically keypad sits above home indicator area (34). I'll place keypad at y=844-34-226=584, home indicator at 810.\n  - So sheet spans from ~y=286 to 584 (height ~298) covering header, field, button. Actually the sheet should visually contain the keypad? The keypad is system UI overlaid; sheet content sits above it. I'll make sheet from y=270 to bottom (844), white with top radius, and keypad placed on top of it at 584..810, home indicator at 810..844. That looks like a sheet with keypad open. \n\n### 03_Home (390×844) bg #F6F7FB\n- Status bar (47).\n- Header (y≈55, h 48): Avatar_Hallie_Goebel instance 40×40 (source 72×72, resize) left x=20; search pill centered: rounded 12, white bg, Icon_Search 18 + text \"Pay by name or phone\" 13 gray, width ~258; right: Icon_History in white circle button 40×40.\n- Balance card (y≈115, x=20, w=350, h≈150): gradient brand (#1E32FA→#4A5BFF? angle 135°), radius 20, white text:\n  - top row: Bank_HSBC instance (75×21, white? bank marks keep brand colors — HSBC logo is red/white hexagon; on blue card may clash. Alternative: put logo in white rounded chip. I'll place logo inside a white rounded rect chip (padding) to preserve brand colors.) \n  - right top: refresh Icon_Refresh white 20px (action \"refresh balance\").\n  - \"Last Updated Balance\" 12/Medium white 70%.\n  -