rder stroke override + separate +91? The +91 prefix must be inside the field box. Can't add nodes into instance. \n\nSo: build my own `Field/Phone/Focused` component that replicates the default Text Field's look (same radius, colors) + brand focus ring + +91 prefix + placeholder. I'll read the default Text Field's styling in script and mirror it. And I'll still place an instance of the given Text Field in my local components sheet? That adds clutter; skip. The given components usage: Button ✓, Status Bar ✓, Home Indicator ✓, Numeric Keypad ✓. Text Field — I'll try to use it; if structure unsuitable, my own. To keep calls low, I'll just build my own phone field and also use the default Button. Fine — \"reuse the components\" mainly = don't rebuild status bar/keypad.\n\nHmm, but let me quickly inspect Button and Text Field in the first build script and log their structure to decide. I can read but output comes back as tool result — I can adapt within the SAME script (conditional logic). E.g., instance Button, find TEXT child, set \"Get Started\", done. That's safe regardless.\n\nMedia components as instances: illustration, avatars, banks (5), merchants (2), icons (13). Icon recolor: override vector fills in instance children.\n\n**Icon usage mapping:**\n- 01: none required.\n- 02: none (Cancel text, field). Icon_Close not required; skip.\n- 03: Icon_Search (search), Icon_History (header), Icon_Refresh (card), Icon_Check_Badge (Primary), Icon_Send, Icon_Receive, Icon_Scan, Icon_Offer (banner). Bank marks ×4, Merchant_Paytm, Avatar_Risa, Merchant_Amazon, Avatar_Hallie.\n- 04: Avatar_Hallie, Icon_New_Payment, Icon_Bank, Icon_History, Icon_Offer, Icon_Settings, Icon_Logout.\n\n**Building with auto-layout vs absolute:** For reliability in code, absolute positioning with manual y-cursor is actually simpler to get pixel-exact and debug. But auto-layout gives professional structure. Mixed: top-level screens absolute (I'll compute y positions), rows/tiles with auto-layout wher