e card: gradientTransform for 135°. Using fills: [{type:'GRADIENT_LINEAR', gradientStops:[{0:#1E32FA},{1:#4B63FF}], gradientTransform}]. I'll use a transform approximating diagonal: [[0.7,0.7,-0.35],[-0.7,0.7,0.85]]? I can compute: for 135deg use gradientTransform [[cos, sin, tx],[-sin, cos, ty]]… easier: use [[1,1,-0.2],[-1,1,0.7]] roughly diagonal. Fine-tune not critical.\n\nAlso add decorative circles on balance card (white 6% circles) for polish.\n\n**Numeric keypad:** given 390×226 — instance at (0,584) in 02. Its bg probably light gray. Good.\n\n**Status bar on dark areas:** 03 top area is light (#F6F7FB) → default dark glyphs fine. 01 white → fine. 02/04: status bar area is scrimmed bg… The status bar instance belongs to the cloned bg (under scrim) — dimmed, fine; or I add status bar above scrim? Keep under scrim (dimmed status bar looks natural for modal). Actually for the sheet/modal, real iOS keeps status bar visible not dimmed when using pageSheet… With full dim + bottom sheet, status bar usually stays visible (black text over dimmed bg? messy). I'll leave the cloned one under the scrim — acceptable.\n\nLet me also handle \"Button\" given component resize: instance.resize may fail if constraints… resize works on instances; internal layout depends on component constraints (probably center). Label override: find text node, set characters after font load (its font might be Inter already — given kit says Inter replaces SF Pro; load Inter anyway).\n\nOne more consideration: **cloning 01 for 02's background** — 01 is a top-level frame on the page. clone() → same parent (page). Then I need to embed into 02: `frame02.appendChild(clone)`. Frame-in-frame fine. Clear reactions recursively. Also remove the home indicator? No—keep full fidelity.\n\nPosition clone at (0,0) inside 02, name \"BG · 01_Onboarding\".\n\nFor 04: clone 03 similarly.\n\nAlright — also **don't forget**: 02's \"Get Started\" button + \"Cancel\" both required actions; Cancel is text button top-right of sheet.\n\nPrototype hotspots:\n- 01: the Get Started instance → reaction to 02.\n- 02: Cancel text → 01; Get Started instance → 03.\n- 03: avatar instance (header) → 04. Put reaction on avatar instance (or wrapping frame \"AvatarButton\").\n- 04: hotspot rect (visible part of 03) → 03. Also maybe clicking scrim area anywhere outside panel = same hotspot covering x312..390 only (visible part). Brief: \"tap the visible part of 03_Home → 03_Home\". Hotspot x=312..390 h=844.\n\nTransition details (duration 0.3, easing EASE_OUT / EASE_IN_OUT).\n\nNow write the scripts. I must be careful with Plugin API correctness:\n\n- `const page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('6:2');` type 'PAGE'. `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)`.\n- Fonts: `await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter', style:'Regular'})` etc.\n- createFrame: figma.createFrame(), set x,y, resize(w,h), fills, clipsContent.\n- Text: figma.createText(), set fontName AFTER load, characters, fontSize, fontName per weight (set fontName = {family:'Inter',style:'Semi Bold'}), fills, lineHeight {unit:'PIXELS', value}, letterSpacing {unit:'PIXELS', value}, textAlignHorizontal.\n- Corner radius: node.cornerRadius.\n- Effects: node.effects = [{type:'DROP_SHADOW', color:{r,g,b,a}, offset:{x,y}, radius, spread, visible:true, blendMode:'NORMAL'}].\n- Strokes: node.strokes=[solid], strokeWeight, strokeAlign.\n- Instance: `(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('4:5')).createInstance()` — must be ComponentNode. Then parent.appendChild(inst); inst.x=..., resize.\n- Reactions: node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId:'6:xxx', navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'UP', duration:{type:'DURATION', value:0.3}, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}, preserveScrollPosition:false, overlayRelativePosition:null? }] — for NAVIGATE action, fields: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition, preserveScrollPosition:false}. I think that shape works. If error, I'll see message.\n\ngetNodeByIdAsync for components on other pages: fine in same doc.\n\ncreateComponent then place into a components frame: comp = figma.createComponent(); compFrame.appendChild(comp); build children into comp; instances: inst=comp.createInstance(); screenFrame.appendChild(inst).\n\nFor component children creation, append to comp before instancing.\n\nSwap nested: `innerInst.swapComponent(targetComp)`.\n\nText measurement: after creating text node and setting properties, node.width/height available synchronously (text layout computed). Yes.\n\nHelper functions per script. Since each use_figma call is separate execution, redefine helpers each time.\n\nEdge: name conflicts none.\n\nAlso set frame names EXACTLY: \"01_Onboarding\", \"02_Phone_Number\", \"03_Home\", \"04_Menu\".\n\nExport settings? Not needed.\n\nLet me now also finalize 03 heights with actual numbers computed in code via cursor variable — I'll write code that stacks with a y-cursor and sets final frame height = cursor + bottomPad. That avoids manual math errors. For the home indicator on 03: place at bottom (y = frameH-34). I'll compute cursor first by creating sections then set frame height and indicator position at end.\n\nFor 01 (fixed 844): positions as planned.\n\nTime to write Call A: switch page, load fonts, inspect given components + a few media nodes (children structure), return JSON summaries. Keep output small: for each of [1:23,1:26,1:33,1:44,1:46]: name, size, children (name/type/size/fill colors/fontSize). Also inspect 4:2, 4:3 (avatars) children types. Also verify Inter fonts load OK.\n\nThen Call B builds 01. Etc.\n\nLet me write Call A now.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a2cffc4-ceaf-40ca-907b-3a7089c49bbf","uuid":"6f9876e3-357c-44bf-b99b-0ff7d4bf6325","timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:51:13.547Z","thinking_duration_ms":417652}
